    trace.string_literal("Hard ceiling on printed rows.\\nWith more weapons than fit, the last row becomes \\\"+N\\\".");
    trace.string_literal("Which row a script fills:\\nmayrr.esp.SetPlayerText(index, slot, text).\\nEmpty slot draws nothing.");
    trace.string_literal("Print name is what the SWEP calls itself (\\\"AK-47\\\").\\nClass name is the entity class (\\\"ttt_m16\\\").\\nA SWEP with no print name falls back to the class.");
    trace.string_literal("How job and team names are compared.\\n\\nExact - case-insensitive equality.\\nContains - either string inside the other. Use this when the\\nserver decorates jobs (\\\"Job [VIP]\\\" against a team named \\\"Job\\\"),\\nwhich under Exact makes EVERY player read as disguised.");
    trace.string_literal("What to print when the job disagrees with the networked team,\\ni.e. when the player is disguised (UnionTeams / JCT keep\\nply:Team() honest and only rewrite the job).\\n\\nShow real team - the long-standing behaviour: reveal what he is.\\nShow job -> real - both, so the lie stays readable too.\\nIgnore - never swap, always print the job.");
